.TH MV 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
mv \- move or rename files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mv
.I from to
.br
.B mv
.IR from ...
.I directory
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mv
renames
.I from
to
.IR to .
If the last operand is a directory, each
.I from
is moved into it, keeping its name; with more than two operands, the last
must be a directory.
.PP
Files and directories (with everything in them) can be moved. Across
filesystems (between disks, or to
.IR /tmp ),
.B mv
copies, then removes the original; symbolic links are copied as links.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if everything was moved; 1 on too few operands, a last operand that is
not a directory when it must be, or if anything could not be moved.
.SH NOTES
There are no options: every word is a file name.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cp (1),
.BR rm (1),
.BR ln (1)
